ro-product-property\u002F",[173,181],{"type":174,"title":150,"items":175},"parent",[176],{"type":177,"title":178,"info":179,"reason":180},"physical","Algebra Word Problems","Anita Harnadek","Huge collection of word problems which lead to an equations with detailed solutions.",{"type":174,"title":15,"items":182},[183],{"type":184,"title":185,"info":186,"link":187,"reason":188},"web","LibreTexts Mathematics","An open and free online collection of mathematics educational materials.","https:\u002F\u002Fmath.libretexts.org\u002F","A large amount of materials and many typical practice problems.",[190],{"contributorId":191,"name":192,"avatarUrl":193},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","\u002Ffile\u002Fcontributors\u002Fgwynerva\u002Favatar.png","group",[196,226,259,297,389],{"type":164,"link":197,"title":198,"description":199,"keyLinks":200,"stats":222},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it\u002F","What is it?","\n    Learn how quadratic equations arise from real-life situations,\n    what quadratic equations and quadratic trinomials are,\n    how they are related, and how to determine whether an equation is quadratic.\n  ",[201,208,216],{"link":202,"schemaName":203,"title":204,"key":205,"seo":206,"description":207},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it\u002F?element=problematic-equations","problems","Quadratic equations in real life",{},{},"Examples of various real-life situations that boil down to quadratic equations.\n          This will make it clear why we need to be able to solve them at all.",{"link":209,"schemaName":210,"title":211,"key":212,"seo":213,"description":215},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it\u002F?element=quadratic-trinomial","accent_term","Quadratic trinomial",{},{"title":214},"What is a quadratic trinomial?","Polynomial with the maximum power of the variable equal to two.\n          Acts as a \"template\" or \"general form\" for all quadratic equations.",{"link":217,"schemaName":210,"title":218,"key":219,"seo":220,"description":221},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it\u002F?element=quadratic-equation","Quadratic equation",{},{},"Any equation that can be reduced to the form of a quadratic trinomial by transformations without losing roots.",{"elements":223},{"accent_term":224,"accent_important":225,"problem":155},2,1,{"type":164,"link":227,"title":228,"description":229,"keyLinks":230,"stats":255},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fincomplete\u002F","With missing terms","\n    Quadratic equations with missing terms (incomplete quadratics) are the simplest forms of quadratic equations where the coefficient B, C, or both are missing.\n    Let's learn how to solve them correctly in each specific case.\n  ",[231,238,246],{"link":232,"schemaName":210,"title":233,"key":234,"seo":235,"description":237},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fincomplete\u002F?element=quadratic-missing-terms","Incomplete quadratic equation",{},{"title":236},"What is an incomplete quadratic equation?","A quadratic equation in which coefficient B or C or both are zero.",{"link":239,"schemaName":240,"title":241,"key":242,"seo":243,"description":245},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fincomplete\u002F?element=solving-incomplete-quadratic-equations","heading","Solving such equations",{},{"title":244},"How to solve incomplete quadratic equations?","Detailed analysis of solving all types of incomplete quadratic equations with derivation of general formulas.",{"link":247,"schemaName":248,"title":249,"key":250,"seo":252,"description":254},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fincomplete\u002F?element=all-formulas","diagram","General formulas for incomplete quadratic equations",{"title":251},"General formulas",{"title":253},"General formulas for solving incomplete quadratic equations","Formulas for all three types of incomplete quadratic equations:\n          when \"B\" and \"C\" are zero, when \"C\" is zero, and when \"B\" is zero.",{"elements":256},{"accent_term":225,"accent_statement":257,"accent_important":225,"problem":258},3,7,{"type":164,"link":260,"title":261,"description":262,"keyLinks":263,"stats":294},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fcompleting-the-square\u002F","Completing the Square","\n    The technique of \"packing\" an expanded expression into a compact squared binomial.\n    This method allows you to solve any quadratic equation!\n    Let's learn how to do it with detailed examples and visualizations.\n  ",[264,271,278,286],{"link":265,"schemaName":210,"title":266,"key":267,"seo":268,"description":270},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fcompleting-the-square\u002F?element=what-is-it","Completing the square",{"title":198},{"title":269},"What is completing the square?","\"Packing\" an expanded expression into a squared binomial.",{"link":272,"schemaName":240,"title":273,"key":274,"seo":275,"description":277},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fcompleting-the-square\u002F?element=why-bother","Why do this?",{},{"title":276},"Why complete the square?","Completing the square is a powerful tool for transforming expressions and solving quadratic equations.",{"link":279,"schemaName":240,"title":280,"key":281,"seo":283,"description":285},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fcompleting-the-square\u002F?element=solving-quadratic-equations","Solving quadratic equations",{"title":282},"Solving equations",{"title":284},"Solving quadratic equations by completing the square","Completing the square is the key to solving absolutely any quadratic equations.",{"link":287,"schemaName":288,"title":289,"key":290,"seo":291,"description":293},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fcompleting-the-square\u002F?element=process-visualization","image","Process visualization",{},{"title":292},"Completing the square visualization","How a large square is literally assembled or \"completed\" from smaller shapes.",{"elements":295},{"accent_term":225,"accent_important":225,"problem":296},11,{"type":164,"link":298,"title":299,"description":300,"keyLinks":301,"stats":386},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F","Quadratic formula","\n    A clear derivation of the quadratic formula with a detailed explanation of every step.\n    Learn what the discriminant is, where it comes from, and how it tells you how many roots a quadratic equation has.\n  ",[302,310,317,325,332,339,347,355,362,370,378],{"link":303,"schemaName":304,"title":305,"key":306,"seo":307,"description":309},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=general-formulas","accent_important","General root formulas",{},{"title":308},"What is a general formula for equation roots?","General root formulas let you solve a whole class of equations by direct substitution.",{"link":311,"schemaName":210,"title":312,"key":313,"seo":314,"description":316},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=discriminant","Discriminant",{},{"title":315},"What is the discriminant of a quadratic equation?","A special number computed from the coefficients of a quadratic equation. It tells you how many roots the equation has.",{"link":318,"schemaName":319,"title":320,"key":321,"seo":323,"description":324},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=formula","accent_statement","The quadratic formula",{"title":322},"Quadratic equation roots",{},"A general formula that lets you find the roots of any quadratic equation by plugging in the coefficients.",{"link":326,"schemaName":210,"title":327,"key":328,"seo":329,"description":331},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=biquadratic","Biquadratic equation",{},{"title":330},"What is a biquadratic equation?","A special type of fourth-degree equation that you can solve by reducing it to a quadratic equation.",{"link":333,"schemaName":304,"title":334,"key":335,"seo":337,"description":338},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=no-general-formulas-above-degree-4","Why there is no general formula for degree 5+",{"title":336},"Limits of formulas",{},"For equations above the 4th degree, there is no universal \"plug in numbers -- get roots\" formula.",{"link":340,"schemaName":248,"title":341,"key":342,"seo":344,"description":346},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=algorithm","Quadratic equation solving algorithm",{"title":343},"Solving algorithm",{"title":345},"How to solve a quadratic equation","A diagram that shows how to solve any quadratic equation step by step.",{"link":348,"schemaName":349,"title":350,"key":351,"seo":352,"description":354},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=deriving-the-quadratic-formula","table","Deriving the quadratic formula",{},{"title":353},"How to derive the quadratic formula","A step-by-step derivation of the quadratic formula with explanations.",{"link":356,"schemaName":203,"title":357,"key":358,"seo":359,"description":361},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=even-coefficient","Even coefficient",{},{"title":360},"quadratic equation with even B coefficient","A simpler root formula for quadratics when the coefficient B is even.",{"link":363,"schemaName":364,"title":365,"key":366,"seo":367,"description":369},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=sridharas-method","problem","Sridhara's method",{},{"title":368},"quadratic formula: Sridhara method","A faster way to derive the quadratic formula, with one small trick.",{"link":371,"schemaName":203,"title":372,"key":373,"seo":374,"description":377},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=quadratic-in-f","Trinomial equation",{},{"title":375,"description":376},"What is a trinomial equation?","Definition of trinomial equations and worked examples of solving them by reducing to a quadratic equation.","A special kind of equation with three terms, where the same \"unknown function\" appears in different powers and the whole thing can be reduced to a quadratic.",{"link":379,"schemaName":203,"title":380,"key":381,"seo":382,"description":385},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fquadratic-formula\u002F?element=palindromials","Reciprocal equation",{},{"title":383,"description":384},"What is a reciprocal (palindromic) equation?","Definition of reciprocal (palindromic) equations and worked examples solved by reducing them to quadratic equations.","A special kind of equation where coefficients mirror each other around the equation's \"center\".",{"elements":387},{"accent_term":224,"accent_statement":225,"accent_important":224,"problem":388},14,{"type":164,"link":390,"title":391,"description":392,"keyLinks":393,"stats":442},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F","Factoring quadratics","\n    Rewriting quadratic trinomials and quadratic equations as a product of factors instead of a sum of terms.\n    Lets you solve equations quickly, simplify messy expressions, and spot the roots immediately.\n  ",[394,400,408,414,421,427,434],{"link":395,"schemaName":304,"title":396,"key":397,"seo":398,"description":399},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=both-plus-and-multiplication-matter","Both plus and multiplication matter!",{},{},"In different situations, you need to be able to write expressions both as sums and as products of factors.",{"link":401,"schemaName":402,"title":403,"key":404,"seo":405,"description":407},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=why-factoring","list","Why bother?",{},{"title":406},"Why is factoring a quadratic trinomial useful?","Factoring quadratic trinomials lets you simplify expressions, see the roots right away, and gives you an alternative way to solve quadratic equations.",{"link":409,"schemaName":240,"title":410,"key":411,"seo":412,"description":413},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=factoring-by-hand","Factoring by hand",{},{},"A method for factoring \"simple\" quadratic trinomials by hand.",{"link":415,"schemaName":319,"title":416,"key":417,"seo":418,"description":420},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=general-factoring","General factoring form",{},{"title":419},"Formula for factoring a quadratic trinomial","If a quadratic trinomial has roots, it can always be factored using those roots.",{"link":422,"schemaName":248,"title":423,"key":424,"seo":425,"description":426},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=factoring-cases","Factoring cases",{},{},"All possible ways a quadratic trinomial can factor.",{"link":428,"schemaName":349,"title":429,"key":430,"seo":431,"description":433},"\u002Fsummary\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Ffactoring\u002F?element=deriving-the-factorization-formula","Deriving the factorization formula",{},{"title":432},"Deriving the factorization formula for a quadratic trinomial","A step-by-step derivation of the factorization formula for a quadratic trinomial, with notes.",{"link":435,"schemaName":203,"title":436,"key":437,"seo":439,"description":441},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u